  ('abb-88caca0d', '2CDS200918R0001', '2CDS200918R0001', 'ABB S2C-NT - Hand Operated Neutral', 'ABB', 'Switchgear', 'The hand operated neutral has to be mounted on the left side of the MCB and be snaped on the DIN rail. It is used for measuring duties where the neutral conductor must be in the open position. Due to the special design of the handle - when switching the MCB ON- the neutral will close before and open after the MCB. Suitable for MCBs S200 series.', 630, 617, 'pc', 'https://shop.in.abb.com/media/catalog/product/6/3/63b5ae421ff926.27527852.jpg', true, true, 11033),
  ('abb-5b4637ba', '2CDS200922R0001', '2CDS200922R0001', 'ABB S2C-S/H6R - Signal / Auxiliary Contact', 'ABB', 'Switchgear', 'Choice through a selector between indication of the position of the device’s contacts and signalling of a fault (overcurrent/short-circuit for MCBs and RCBOs, earth fault for RCCBs and RCBOs). Suitable for MCBs S 200 series, SN 201 series, RCCBs F 200 series, RCBOs DS201, DS202C, DS 200 series.', 935, 916, 'pc', 'https://shop.in.abb.com/media/catalog/product/6/3/63b5ae4b8ffb50.54333043.jpg', true, true, 11034),
  ('abb-cde61173', '2CDS252001R0065', '2CDS252001R0065', 'ABB Miniature Circuit Breaker - S200 - 2P - B - 6 ampere', 'ABB', 'Switchgear', 'System pro M compact S200 miniature circuit breakers are current limiting. They have two different tripping mechanisms, the delayed thermal tripping mechanism for overload protection and the electromechanic tripping mechanism for short circuit protection. They are available in different characteristics (B,C,D,K,Z), configurations (1P,1P+N,2P,3P,3P+N,4P), breaking capacities (up to 6 kA at 230/400 ', 3340, 3273, 'pc', 'https://shop.in.abb.com/media/catalog/product/6/3/63b5ae5e95fe32.38667064.png', true, true, 11035),
  ('abb-181dc327', '2CDS251001R0024', '2CDS251001R0024', 'ABB Miniature Circuit Breaker - S200 - 1P - C - 2 ampere', 'ABB', 'Switchgear', 'System pro M compact S200 miniature circuit breakers are current limiting. They have two different tripping mechanisms, the delayed thermal tripping mechanism for overload protection and the electromechanic tripping mechanism for short circuit protection. They are available in different characteristics (B,C,D,K,Z), configurations (1P,1P+N,2P,3P,3P+N,4P), breaking capacities (up to 6 kA at 230/400 ', 1599, 1567, 'pc', 'https://shop.in.abb.com/media/catalog/product/6/3/63b5ae68d61e96.01231828.png', true, true, 11036),
